# global-secrets-evidence

> **Purpose:** Protect trust: no key ever leaks, and no provider fact enters the code without a source.
>
> **Applies to:** Every file in the repo (always on).

## Secrets
- Never commit `.env` files. Commit `.env.example` only, with empty values.
- Never log, return or print an API key.
- Only `apps/api` calls OpenAI, Tavily or provider endpoints. The browser never does.
- Every `VITE_` variable is public. Never put a secret in one.

## Evidence
- Never invent provider facts in code, prompts, fixtures or library JSON.
- Every provider fact needs a source URL and a verbatim quote.
- If a fact cannot be sourced, label it Uncertain.
- Time estimates stay Uncertain until tested.

## Docs are the source of truth
- Read the matching file in `docs/` before changing a feature.
- Update that doc in the same change when behaviour changes.
- Never build anything on the Won't list in `docs/features.md`.
